; Tutorial_6_Rename_Files_to_What_Is_Inside.inix -- naming files after what they hold.

[about]
Title=6 - Rename Files to What Is Inside
Intro=One want: files named by a camera or a scanner, called by what they are instead. FileDir reads each tagged file's own title -- a PDF's, a song's, a photograph's caption, a book's name -- and renames the file after it.
Setup=A folder holds downloaded files with names that say nothing.
Homework=Tag a few downloaded PDFs and rename them to what is inside; then check each new name with Down Arrow.


[step]

Say=One want: files with names that say nothing -- IMG underscore 4021, Scan 7 -- called by what they are. A file often carries its own title inside it; FileDir can read it and rename the file after it.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Alt plus Control plus F opens FileDir on the folder it last showed.
Key=Alt+Control+F
Hear=FileDir

[step]

Say=Walk four showed tagging. I tag the files to rename: the semicolon tags the current one.
Key=Semicolon
Hear=Tagged

[step]

Say=Down Arrow to the next, and the semicolon again.
Key=Semicolon
Hear=2 tagged files

[step]

Say=Control plus Shift plus I, I for Identify, renames each tagged file after what is inside it. FileDir asks first, showing each old name beside its new one.
Key=Control+Shift+I
Hear=Rename to Identify Content dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=It looked in the metadata first: a PDF's title, a song's name, a photograph's caption, choosing the longest title-like field, so Sunset over the Cascades wins over IMG underscore 4021. Enter accepts.
Key=Enter
Hear=2 files renamed
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=A planned misstep: a text file with no metadata. FileDir falls back on its first line, which may be a date or a byline rather than a title. I tag one and try.
Key=Semicolon
Hear=Tagged

[step]

Say=Control plus Shift plus I.
Key=Control+Shift+I
Hear=Rename to Identify Content dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=The proposed name is a date. Escape cancels, and nothing is renamed; F2 renames the file by hand instead.
Key=Escape
Hear=FileDir
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=What this walk taught. I name the step; the reader gives the key.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Tag a file.
Key=
Hear=Semicolon

[step]

Say=Rename tagged files after what is inside them.
Key=
Hear=Control plus Shift plus I

[step]

Say=Rename one file by hand.
Key=
Hear=F2
